# Terms that must never appear in this repo. One per line, case-insensitive,
# substring match. `#` starts a comment.
#
# Copy this file to `.private-terms` and fill in your own. `.private-terms` is
# gitignored on purpose: a list of your clients' names is itself the thing you
# are trying to keep out of a public repo.
#
# Put in it: client and employer names, their product names, real prospect
# companies, live campaign ids, internal tool or table names, teammates' names.
#
# tests/test_no_private_data.py fails the build if any of them appear in a
# git-tracked file. Without this file that check is skipped and says so.

